[
    {
        "content": "<p>I have been experimenting with a version of the <code>change</code> tactic that besides changing the type to another defeq one, also \"renames\" the named holes you supply (like <code>?a</code>) as newly introduced local declarations <code>a : type := expr</code>. My motivation was to have a quick way to refer to subexpressions of the goal or local declarations, without having to <code>set :=</code> a possibly very big expression. It should also be more robust than <code>set</code> because it matches on the structure of the expression modulo defeq.</p>\n<p>A small example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">change_set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- we get a := 1, b := instOfNatNat 0 and ⊢ (fun x =&gt; 0 + a) b = a</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">change_set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- we get c := 0, d := 0 and this : c + d = d</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This was also an exercise for me to learn more about how those internals work.</p>",
        "id": 597849941,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1779803118
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"548935\">@Thomas Murrills</span> this is basically <code>setm</code> + <code>change</code>. I would prefer that we omit the <code>change</code> feature so that we don't abuse defeq with this. But I thought you would have some thing to say here. At the very least, we should dig up the old <code>setm</code> thread.</p>",
        "id": 597850802,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1779803303
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>To be clear: I would like to see <code>setm</code> in Mathlib very soon.</p>",
        "id": 597850938,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1779803333
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Would making it not abuse defeq be a matter of wrapping it in <code>withReducible / withReducibleAndInstances</code>?</p>",
        "id": 597854684,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1779804170
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yes, something to that effect.</p>",
        "id": 597867180,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1779807111
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But <code>change</code> specifically allows for semireducible (i.e., default) transparency. So then the connection to <code>change</code> doesn't really exist. This is why I was distinguishing between <code>setm</code> and <code>change</code>.</p>",
        "id": 597867516,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1779807184
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>edit: the original <code>setm</code> has a pr here : <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/7890\">#7890</a>.</p>",
        "id": 597869080,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1779807546
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>and making it <code>withReducibleAndInstances</code> is probably necessary, because otherwise it sometimes comes up with a weird type for the variable like <code>Option NNReal</code> instead of <code>ENNReal</code></p>",
        "id": 597872162,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1779808249
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"571941\">@Lua Viana Reis</span> please see the prior thread which I've just found: <a href=\"#narrow/channel/239415-metaprogramming-.2F-tactics/topic/Help.20with.20writing.20tactic.20.60setm.60\">#metaprogramming / tactics &gt; Help with writing tactic &#96;setm&#96;</a>.</p>",
        "id": 597873372,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1779808536
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There is a lot in there, but the current <code>change</code> still has the trouble with the <code>?a</code> being <code>syntheticOpaque</code>, e.g. this fails:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">change</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 597879483,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1779810081
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>and my hope was for this tactic to work under binders, for now it works with constants under binders but I would like to make it replace expressions referring to the local variables as well (make them function applications)</p>",
        "id": 597885320,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1779811567
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have to point out some hygiene issues with (ab)using named metavariables in this way. I think that one should avoid them to avoid hygiene issues. See my <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/7890#issuecomment-4580617687\">comment to #7890</a> which demonstrates a named metavariable collision. See also <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"217875\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/reuse.20previous.20goals.3F/with/524939719\">#Is there code for X? &gt; reuse previous goals?</a></p>",
        "id": 598659491,
        "sender_full_name": "Niklas Halonen",
        "timestamp": 1780097140
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Interesting, the code I had posted on the first message in this thread was replacing the syntax of the named holes with something else along with a custom elaborator, so that they got assigned other type of metavariables, but it had other problems. But perhaps this idea could be used to avoid this</p>",
        "id": 598701297,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1780132481
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>the code, for reference (I am not advocating for it)</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span>\n<span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Rewrite</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- A pattern hole that captures the matched expression under the name `n`.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    Behaves like `_` for elaboration purposes (natural mvar, current lctx),</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    but records the resulting `MVarId` so the surrounding tactic can recover</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    the captured value. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">captureHole</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"capture% \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">capturePrefix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`_setm</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">term_elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">captureHole</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elabCaptureHole</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TermElab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expectedType?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">capture</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">throwUnsupportedSyntax</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">capturePrefix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getId</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decl</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getMCtx</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">decls</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decl</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">userName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mvar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">mkFreshExprMVar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expectedType?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">userName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Rewrite every `?ident` in a syntax tree to `capture% ident`; leave `?_`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    and everything else untouched. -/</span>\n<span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rewriteNamedHoles</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">StateT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NameSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MacroM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getKind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``Lean.Parser.Term.syntheticHole</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isIdent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkIdent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getId</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">modify</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">insert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><spa